   "confidence": "low",
   "notes": "Old Cavendish Laboratory (W.M. Fawcett, 1872-4), Free School Lane front: buff ashlar Gothic Revival. Deep ogee-arched carriage archway with crocketed finial, heraldic panels and a statue niche (of the Duke of Devonshire) above; small oriel over the arch; red pillar box beside it. Three bays of two-light stone-mullioned windows with hood moulds on three storeys and gabled stone dormers in the roof. Archway placed at the south end of the wall; bay positions estimated from two Commons close-ups."
